    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d682">

                <pb facs="0972" n="962" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg962"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3–846: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-03-08T10:00:00+07:00">March 8, 1946—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>451. From General Marshall. I agree with Eximbank terms with exception that I
                    recommend China be given 3 (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) terms (Reurtel 389
                    of March 2) on the 10 million dollars of China’s requisitions approved but not
                    contracted for by US. [Marshall.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
